hilde (1.0) stable; urgency=low

  * The compiler reports 1.0.0.
  * Language: pattern matching in case, and a case over integers becomes a
    C switch; error kinds in the signature with raises and raise; the type
    Never for a function that does not come back, and slots that one
    module of a programme implements; an argument takes the type of its
    parameter; read through a write reference.
  * Contracts after Ada: requires and ensures checked at run time,
    invariants of records, random tests made from the contracts by
    hilde test, and simple cases proved when the programme is compiled.
    Every public function of the standard library states its contracts.
  * Commands: hilde check, hilde fmt, hilde lsp, hilde query, hilde test
    with --memory, --race and --valgrind, and hilde guard.  A stable code
    for every error, and the messages also in rustc's JSON.
  * Packages: hilde-pkg, started by hilde get, update, verify, export,
    new, install and doc; versions from git tags with Minimal Version
    Selection, hilde.sum with a checksum of the tree and a signify key
    taken on first use, vendor/ checked in, capabilities held by hilde
    guard, the API diff with contracts, doc tests and manual pages.
  * Sperli: a job of ranks on listed hosts that send each other messages
    with a tag, every connection TLS 1.3 with certificates on both sides,
    started by the launcher hilde-launcher or hilde run.
  * Targets: static and shared libraries with a header, WebAssembly, and C
    for another machine; built for Android and iOS.
  * Runtime: tasks on fibers with scopes, joined handles and bounded
    channels; the runtime built and run on Linux, OpenBSD, FreeBSD and
    macOS; a programme confines itself with pledge and unveil, Landlock and
    seccomp, Capsicum or Seatbelt.
  * Standard library: Regex with RE2 syntax, Pcre with the JIT under W^X,
    Map, Sort, Text over spans, Json, Csv, Ini, Yaml, Xml, Cbor, Base64,
    Gzip, Decimal, Calendar with time zones, Log, Signal, Arguments after
    clap, Paths and Platform.
  * Standard library: SQLite with SQL checked against the migrations,
    SQLCipher, PostgreSQL, MariaDB and DuckDB behind Standard.Database,
    with drivers a programme imports only when it needs them; Search,
    Session, Users, Cache, Raft and SQLite replicated through it.
  * Standard library: Tls as client and server with client certificates,
    HttpClient, FastCGI, Smtp, Sftp and commands over SSH, Resolve,
    templates with Jinja2 syntax compiled with the programme,
    translations, an HTML sanitizer and htmx.
  * Standard library: libcrypto with AEAD, X25519, Ed25519, RSA, ECDSA and
    ML-DSA, X.509 and ACME, JWS and one-time passwords, Argon2 and the
    check of old bcrypt hashes, Vault for secrets in an environment file,
    Secret read from the terminal, PNG and QR codes.
  * Tooling: editor support for Vim, Emacs, VS Code and Zed, and a
    tree-sitter grammar; a guide for learning Hilde and a list of traps.
  * Checks: on Linux a second compiler, the Clang Static
    Analyzer, cppcheck, AddressSanitizer, UBSan, valgrind and AFL++, and
    0 warnings under three yardsticks; the same tests on OpenBSD 8.0,
    FreeBSD and macOS.

 -- Heiko Zimmermann <code@heiko-zimmermann.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100

hilde (0.3.0) stable; urgency=low

  * The first release of the fork, from Austral 0.2.0.
  * The language is renamed Hilde: module bodies .hiq, interfaces .hih,
    the command hilde.
  * Generated C is compiled with -std=c17 -Wall -Wextra and carries the
    names the source used.
  * The module order is computed from the imports; the C compiler is run
    without a shell.
  * @embed only in a module that carries pragma Unsafe_Module, and an
    application can forbid unsafe modules.
  * The ? operator and ignore(): a discarded Option or Either is a type
    error.  Float32 arithmetic, @bytes, --line-directives, and
    pragma Foreign_Library with the tool gen-bindings.
  * Standard library modules Arena, Text, Ip, Http, Fcgi, Sandbox, File,
    Poller, Path, Utf8 and Time.
  * Fixed: Buffer.bump copied from freed memory, modular arithmetic
    depended on -fwrapv, ByteSize literals above 255, region erasure for
    monomorph keys, Box used Left for success, overlapping instances,
    hilde_abort was not _Noreturn, and the compiler did not work on
    OpenBSD.

